{
  "id": "giving",
  "kind": "api",
  "title": "Tithe.ly Giving",
  "description": "Tithe.ly giving — live donors and real money — Weekly giving reports for Grace Church",
  "credential": {
    "label": "Tithe.ly API keys",
    "description": "The public and private key pair for this connection's environment. API access is by request: email support@tithe.ly to have keys issued. Test keys work only against tithelydev.com and live keys only against tithe.ly.",
    "fields": [
      {
        "name": "publicKey",
        "label": "Public key",
        "description": "Starts with pub_. Sent as the HTTP Basic user name.",
        "placeholder": "pub_…",
        "inputType": "text"
      },
      {
        "name": "privateKey",
        "label": "Private key",
        "description": "Starts with pri_. Sent as the HTTP Basic password; never expose it in a browser.",
        "placeholder": "pri_…",
        "inputType": "password"
      }
    ]
  },
  "guide": {
    "summary": "Live giving: donor-data reduction, cents and ISO dates, cursor paging, and the form-encoded write hatch.",
    "content": "# Tithe.ly giving usage\n\nLive Tithe.ly (tithe.ly): real donors and real money.\n\nAccount purpose: Weekly giving reports for Grace Church\n\n## Giving data is sensitive\n\n- Donor names, emails, addresses, and gift amounts are pastoral data. Reduce\n  inside `execute_code`: page, filter, and total there, and return the\n  aggregate (sums by fund, month, or donor count), not donor rows, unless the\n  task needs named people.\n- Organization projections omit the payout bank's last four and the legal\n  contact's date of birth.\n  Every result, `raw: true` and the hatches included, leaves them out.\n\n## Ids and vocabulary\n\n- Ids carry their kind: `org_` organization, `user_` donor account,\n  `ch_` charge, `rc_` recurring gift, `pm_` payment method. Read them\n  from `list_organizations` and `list_accounts`; never guess one.\n- A fund is a Tithe.ly giving type: `giving_type` becomes `fund`.\n- Projections rename snake_case to camelCase, return amounts as integer\n  `…Cents`, and Unix-second dates as ISO 8601 UTC `…At`.\n  `depositedAt` may be `\"pending\"`. There is no deposits resource: net\n  amount and fees live on each charge.\n\n## Paging\n\nList tools return `page.hasMore` and `page.nextCursor`; pass the cursor\nback unchanged with the same `order`. `list_charges` and\n`list_recurring_charges` need `organizationId` or `accountId`.\n`list_payment_methods` is not paged.\n\n## Failures\n\nTithe.ly answers most refusals with HTTP 200, `status: \"fail\"`, and a\nreason but no code. They arrive as `connector_call_failed`; read the reason\nrather than retrying blind.\n\n## Writes go through the mutate hatch\n\nEvery Tithe.ly write moves money or changes a donor's payment state, so none\nhas a named tool. `tithely_api_mutate` sends form fields as name/value pairs\nand always needs approval. Amounts are integer cents; card and bank tokens\ncome only from Tithely.js in a browser, never from an agent.\n\n- `POST /charges`: account_id, pm_id, organization_id, amount,\n  giving_type, optional memo. `POST /charge-once` charges a Tithely.js token\n  without an account.\n- `POST /refunds/{charge_id}` refunds a charge.\n- `POST /recurring`: account_id, pm_id, organization_id, amount,\n  giving_type, term (weekly, monthly, bimonthly, fortnightly), start_date\n  (Unix seconds). `DELETE /recurring/{recurring_id}` stops future charges and\n  refunds nothing.\n- `POST /payment-methods` (account_id, token), `POST\n  /payment-methods/{pm_id}` (account_id plus fields to change), `DELETE\n  /payment-methods/{pm_id}` with query account_id.\n- `POST /accounts` and `POST /accounts/{account_id}` create and update\n  donor accounts.\n\n## Limits\n\nTithe.ly publishes no rate limit, so this connection declares no call budget.\nAn operator who knows one sets `callAdmission` on the connection. Only v1 is\nreachable; Tithe.ly's undocumented v2 is not.\n"
  },
  "tools": [
    {
      "name": "tithely_api_get",
      "description": "Call any Tithe.ly v1 GET endpoint and return its response, less the sensitive fields this connection drops. Prefer named reads.",
      "inputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "path": {
            "type": "string",
            "minLength": 1,
            "maxLength": 512,
            "description": "Path below /api/v1 beginning with '/', such as /charges-list or /refunds/ch_123. No query string."
          },
          "query": {
            "type": "array",
            "maxItems": 50,
            "description": "Query parameters as name/value pairs, e.g. account_id.",
            "items": {
              "type": "object",
              "properties": {
                "name": {
                  "type": "string",
                  "minLength": 1,
                  "description": "Tithe.ly's snake_case parameter name."
                },
                "value": {
                  "type": [
                    "string",
                    "number",
                    "boolean"
                  ],
                  "description": "Parameter value; stringified once by the transport."
                }
              },
              "required": [
                "name",
                "value"
              ],
              "additionalProperties": false
            }
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "path"
        ],
        "additionalProperties": false
      },
      "outputSchema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
          "result": {
            "description": "Tithe.ly's response body, less the sensitive fields this connection drops, or null when empty."
          }
        },
        "required": [
          "result"
        ]
      },
      "annotations": {
        "readOnlyHint": true
      }
    },
